 "target_mrna_qc_reading": "Pre-stated in D135-S0(8), before the numbers were seen: a shRNA failure and a CRISPR failure do not mean the same thing. shRNA degrades the transcript, so reduced mRNA is the direct expected readout and a failure is evidence the knockdown did not work. CRISPR disrupts the GENE; a frameshift transcript escaping nonsense-mediated decay leaves mRNA near normal while the protein is gone, so a CRISPR perturbation can be fully effective with no mRNA movement. A CRISPR mRNA-QC failure is NOT a failed perturbation and is never scored as one. Only 48 of the 377 targets are L1000 landmark genes; for the rest the 'measured' mRNA is a best-inferred model output, which weakens the QC further.",
